      "problem": "Calculate the slope of the line that passes through the points $(-2,-4)$ and $(-8,-6).$",
      "worked_solution": "We let $({x}_{1},{y}_{1})=(-2,-4)$ and $({x}_{2},{y}_{2})=(-8,-6),$ and compute the slope using the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}m & =\\frac{{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}}{{x}_{2}-{x}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{-6-(-4)}{-8-(-2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{-2}{-6} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the slope is $m=\\frac{1}{3}.$",
